From: Codex <codex@local.invalid>
Subject: [PATCH] sepolicy: label the 4.14 platform-bus sysfs paths

Use existing hardware-specific types for the actual 4.14 paths.
The old /devices/soc rules do not label /devices/platform/soc.
No allow rules, types, permissive domains or init behavior change.

--- a/sepolicy/vendor/genfs_contexts
+++ b/sepolicy/vendor/genfs_contexts
@@ -19,3 +19,29 @@
 
 genfscon sysfs /devices/soc/800f000.qcom,spmi/spmi-0/spmi0-02/800f000.qcom,spmi:qcom,pmi8998@2:gpio-leds/leds/button-backlight/brightness    u:object_r:sysfs_graphics:s0
 genfscon sysfs /devices/soc/800f000.qcom,spmi/spmi-0/spmi0-03/800f000.qcom,spmi:qcom,pmi8998@3:qcom,leds@d000/leds/rgb/rgb_blink    u:object_r:sysfs_graphics:s0
+
+# Labels for the downstream 4.14 platform-bus device paths.
